<title>THAILAND: Bank of Thailand to choose primary dealers in Nov.</title>
<headline>Bank of Thailand to choose primary dealers in Nov.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Thailand (BOT) will for the first time choose primary dealers to trade bonds for it by the end of November, a central bank official said on Monday.</p>
<p>Paibool Kittisrikangwan of the central bank's banking department told reporters the move was a part of the BOT's effort to increase its efficiency in managing liquidity through open market operations.</p>
<p>The deadline for aplications was October 31. The central bank plans to choose 10-15 financial institutions which will buy and sell bonds for it.</p>
<p>These included local and foreign commercial banks, finance companies and securities companies, he said.</p>
<p>-- Bangkok newsroom (662) 652-0642 reuter ak/ram</p>
